# This file maps the `SwiftPlatformExecutors` availability macros of the
# `_PlatformExecutorsCore` module to the `SwiftStdlib` macros of
# availability-macros.def.
#
# The sources of `_PlatformExecutorsCore` are in the swift-platform-executors
# repository, which keys the macros by the package version that first includes
# a declaration:
#
#     @available(SwiftPlatformExecutors 0.1.0, *)
#
# In the toolchain, a declaration is available from the Swift release that
# first includes that package version. Each line maps a package version to the
# `SwiftStdlib` macro of that release, and the build defines the
# `SwiftPlatformExecutors` macro with the availability of that `SwiftStdlib`
# macro.
#
# When update-checkout picks up a version of swift-platform-executors that uses
# a new `SwiftPlatformExecutors` version, add a line for it. Otherwise the build
# of `_PlatformExecutorsCore` fails with "reference to undefined version".

SwiftPlatformExecutors 0.1.0:SwiftStdlib 6.5
